+`/fork` and the fork action on an answer keep that answer in the new session.
+OpenCode excludes the record named by `before`.
+`transcriptCutAfterMessage` selects the first turn boundary after the answer.
+A boundary can be a prompt, compaction, background result, or workflow report.
+With no later boundary, these actions copy the whole transcript.
+A cut visible locally can still be missing on the server.
+An explicit cut retries a 404 once with the same cut and captured runtime.
+A failed retry returns the error to the user.
+
+### Why BTW copies the latest server history
+
+BTW omits `before` so OpenCode snapshots its latest history, including progress in the running turn.
+Creation does not require a completed answer or locally loaded messages.
+The inherited-history marker comes from the cloned transcript before its boundary note is appended.
+The new session records its creation time, and the parent continues independently.
+Future parent updates stay outside that snapshot.
 
